Sequence Diagram
A Sequence Diagram is a UML (Unified Modeling Language) diagram used to show how objects interact with each other in a sequence over time.
It represents:


Messages exchanged between objects


Order of execution


Flow of communication


It is mainly used in:


Software design


System analysis


Object-oriented modeling



Definition
A Sequence Diagram shows:


Interaction between objects


Time sequence of messages


Execution flow from top to bottom


It focuses on “who communicates with whom and in what order.”

Main Components of Sequence Diagram
1. Actor
Represents the user or external system interacting with the application.
Symbol:
Stick figure
Example:


Customer


Student


Admin


6

2. Object / Participant
Represents objects participating in communication.
Symbol:
Rectangle with object name
Example:


Login Page


Database


Payment System



3. Lifeline
Represents the existence of an object during interaction.
Symbol:
Vertical dotted line below object
6

4. Activation Bar
Represents the time an object is active or executing.
Symbol:
Thin vertical rectangle on lifeline

5. Message
Represents communication between objects.
Types of Messages:


Synchronous message


Asynchronous message


Return message


Symbol:
Arrow
Example:
User → Login Page : Enter Username
7

6. Return Message
Represents response back to sender.
Symbol:
Dashed arrow
Example:
Database → System : Login Success

7. Self Message
Object sends message to itself.
Example:
Validate Password internally

8. Destruction
Represents object termination.
Symbol:
X mark at end of lifeline

Advantages of Sequence Diagram


Easy to understand system interaction


Shows order of execution clearly


Useful for debugging and design


Helps developers understand object communication



Limitations


Large systems become complicated


Time-consuming for detailed systems


Does not show complete system structure



Example: Login System Sequence Diagram
Flow:


User enters username/password


Login page sends request to server


Server checks database


Database returns result


System shows success/failure


